        "query_signature": "The learner is causal and feasible. After each action it receives one valid subgradient $g_t$. A Bregman projection/proximal-subproblem interface for $\\psi$ is explicitly available. Inputs $X,\\|\\cdot\\|,\\|\\cdot\\|_*,\\psi,R_\\psi,G_*,T,x_{\\mathrm{init}}$ are public. Past feedback may be stored and reused computationally; no additional historical or sample queries are available beyond the explicitly declared interface.",
